WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.701
to "The Tonight Show"!
You're here!

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:07.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Than you for watching at home.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:10.467
I want to wish everyone
a very happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.934
Happy Thanksgiving, everyone.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:16.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:19.033
By now, your pants have
completed their journey from on

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.767
to unbuttoned
to "Who needs pants?"

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.868
So congratulations.
Please get comfortable.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.234
Relax.
You just did all the dishes.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:27.868
Or you stood around
pretending to be busy

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:30.400
to avoid doing the dishes,
whatever you did.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.133
And, actually, I'd like to make

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:34.100
a quick public-service
announcement, if I could.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.367
If you're still at someone's
house watching me right now,

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.801
everyone wants you to go home.

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:40.667
[ Laughter ]
Goodbye.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.367
Go.
It's time.

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.901
Of course, Thanksgiving was
a little different this year.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:52.501
Your cousin, who was super
into crypto last Thanksgiving,

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.133
not so chatty anymore, right?

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:57.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.300
It's a big night.
Not only is it Thanksgiving,

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.100
but we're coming to you
after tonight's game

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.300
between the Minnesota Vikings
and the New England Patriots.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.234
The Patriots playing
on Thanksgiving makes sense

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:09.033
because most people started
the day looking like this.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.934
And then after all
the eating and stress,

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.634
they end up looking like this.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:13.834
And, uh...

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:17.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:19.634
Some relatives
wanted to watch football,

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.434
others wanted to watch
the World Cup,

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:22.701
while your one creepy nephew

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.234
wanted everyone
to watch "Dahmer."

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.534
And you go, "No."

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.334
Well, get this. I read that
because of inflation,

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.067
the cost of this year's
Thanksgiving dinner

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.634
was up about 20%.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.033
It was tough,
especially if you love

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:36.133
basting your turkey
with premium gasoline.

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:41.567
Meanwhile, Turkey was nearly
75% more expensive.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.601
Yeah. Let's just say
if you ate a turducken,

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.033
the "tur" might've been turtle.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.300
I actually saw that,
due to rising prices of turkey

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:53.067
and other meats, a lot of people
served plant-based alternatives.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:54.667
-Ooh.
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.501
So if you want to know
why Arby's and Taco Bell

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:58.234
are open on Thanksgiving,
that's why.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:01.601
But it's not just inflation.

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:03.534
Turkeys were also
harder to come by

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.334
'cause of a bird-flu outbreak.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:07.634
Everything else going around.

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:10.601
Just to be safe, people also
serve masked potatoes.

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:13.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.467
You guys see -- Masked.
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.334
-Masked.
-Masked -- thank you.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.434
Masked potatoes.
-M-A-S-K -- masked.

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:20.701
-That's a joke for everybody.
-Not mashed.

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.400
-No, no.
-Masked.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.734
-Did you see this, Higgins?

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:26.434
Frank's RedHot just released
an injector

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:28.868
to help you get hot sauce
into your turkey this year.

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.534
Look at this thing.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:31.567
-Oh.

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.234
It's a great way
to spice up your turkey.

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.667
And if you mix
in a little Pfizer,

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.534
even better way to get
your uncle vaccinated.

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:37.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:41.200
"Just have some more turkey.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.801
White meat or dark --
Breast?"

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:45.601
[ Applause ]

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:47.534
This is wild.
I saw a survey that said

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.834
this Thanksgiving,
a third of Americans serve food

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.634
infused with cannabis.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.234
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.133
Yep, weed
and operating a deep-fryer --

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.334
what could possibly go wrong?

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.534
'Course, weed's always been
a part of Thanksgiving.

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:02.033
The Pilgrims were so stoned,
they put buckles on their hats.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.067
I mean, come on.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:06.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.501
Also, it's probably
not the best day to be high.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.868
It's like, "Dude,
I swear I saw a 50-foot

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:13.267
Pillsbury Doughboy
floating down Sixth Avenue."

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:15.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:17.634
Meanwhile, another poll said
that on Thanksgiving,

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:21.200
36% of Americans admit
to drinking more than usual.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.868
You know you drank too much
when there's enough

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.467
empty wine boxes to build
a fort, don't you think?

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:27.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:30.167
But all jokes aside, we have
so much to be thankful for.

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:32.300
We live in the greatest
nation on Earth.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.434
We're --

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:36.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.834
We're making it
through a pandemic.

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:41.601
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:44.000
-And no matter
what channel you watch,

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.801
there's a commercial
featuring Shaq.

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:46.968
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:50.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.033
There's so much to be
grateful for these days.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.801
I think we should take a moment
and go around

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.734
and say what we're thankful for.
I will start.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:04:00.133
I am thankful for my family,
my friends, and this video.

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:02.734
-Ugh!
Oh, my gosh.

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:04.434
Ugh!
What do I do?

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:05.501
[ Burps ]

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:09.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.467
-What about you?
What about you, Higgins?

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:13.601
-Well, I'm thankful
for my kids and my wife

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.200
and this video.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.400
-[ Inhales, coughs ]

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.701
[ Laughter ]
-Man

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:21.701
Okay.
Yeah.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:24.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:27.200
That's interesting. Yeah.
What about you, Tariq?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.801
-Well, I'm thankful
for my bandmates, my fans...

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:34.200
-Yeah.
-...and this video.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.868
-I got these new boots.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:43.501
-And finally, Quest,
what about you?

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:47.934
-I'm thankful for my relatives,
my friends, and this video.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:48.934
-Bye!

00:04:48.934 --> 00:04:50.501
-[ Screaming ]

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:53.334
[ Laughter ]
-[Bleep] [bleep]

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:56.100
-What?
What?!

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.400
[ Applause ]

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.100
It's important to give thanks.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.534
Hey, this is fun.
Today, the 96th Annual

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:08.167
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade
aired on NBC.

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:11.367
96.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:13.634
I was there. We were there.
The Roots and I

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.033
were at the -- at the parade.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.901
I was honored to be performing
at the parade,

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:18.334
although it was tough
when kids were shouting,

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.200
"Jimmy, we loved your balloon!"
and I had to tell them,

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.834
"I don't have a balloon.
That's just my head."

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:23.767
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:26.434
-The parade was great, although,
sadly, after a gust of wind,

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:28.501
the Chase
from "Paw Patrol" balloon

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.100
was neutered
by the Empire State Building.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.567
[ Laughter ]
Terrible.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.868
It's unfortunate.

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:36.067
That's right.
The parade had 16 balloons,

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:38.400
28 floats, 12 marching bands,

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.801
and get this,
more than 700 clowns.

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:42.200
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.367
But it got weird
when Macy's said...

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:45.934
"We didn't hire any clowns."

00:05:45.934 --> 00:05:49.901
-♪ Ring around the rosie ♪

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:53.367
♪ Pocket full of posies ♪

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:55.334
♪ Ashes -- ♪

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:56.734
-Thank you.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.601
Of course, Thanksgiving marks
the official start

00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:00.100
of the holiday shopping season,

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.634
but I heard that, this year,
Walmart, Target, and Best Buy

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:05.334
were all closed for the day.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:08.033
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:10.100
That's right.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.133
They told their employees,
"Take the day off.

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:14.601
We don't want to see you here
until 12:01 a.m.

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:15.968
Okay, good."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.968 --> 00:06:17.634
And, finally,
according to a new survey,

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:19.200
a decent night of sleep

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:22.834
is at the top of most
Americans' holiday wish list.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:24.734
So if you made it
through my monologue,

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:27.934
you're getting sleepy.
You're getting sleepy.

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:29.567
But you're gonna
want to stick around

00:06:29.567 --> 00:06:32.834
because Jerry Seinfeld is here
tonight!

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:35.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.200
Jerry Seinfeld!

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.267
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:42.701
Adam Devine is on the show
this evening!

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:48.968
And we got a performance
from Bruce Springsteen tonight!

00:06:48.968 --> 00:06:50.868
We have a great show.
Let's go write some

00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:52.400
thank-you notes.
Come on, everybody.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:58.000
-♪ I'm down for one more
turkey sandwich ♪

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:04.234
♪ I'm holding out for one more
turkey sandwich ♪

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:07.234
-Oh, my goodness.
Happy Thanksgiving, everybody.

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:08.901
I hope everyone had a great day.

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:11.734
Today is just about over,
and I, uh -- I just thought

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:14.667
I'd take a look
at my Thanksgiving Bingo card.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.968
-Oh.
-Might as well.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.434
Yeah, I already had dinner.
Let's see how I did here.

00:07:18.434 --> 00:07:20.467
Okay, first up,
in this square, we have...

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:25.033
Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.033 --> 00:07:28.133
"Devon?
Oh, it's Taran."

00:07:28.133 --> 00:07:29.868
This next square says...

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:35.067
Ah!
A lot of summer soaps.

00:07:35.067 --> 00:07:37.501
Some are real.
Who knows?

00:07:37.501 --> 00:07:38.701
So I got -- I'm two for two
on that one.

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:40.834
-Two for two, dude.
-Yeah.

00:07:40.834 --> 00:07:42.634
Let's see this next square here.

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:48.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:49.767
-Mid.
-Mid.

00:07:49.767 --> 00:07:51.400
-Wow.
-Didn't happen to me.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.067
Let's take a look
at this next one here.

00:07:57.701 --> 00:07:59.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.400
"Hey, dude."
-"Hey, man."

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.334
-"What are we eatin', man?"
-"Big turkey, dude."

00:08:04.334 --> 00:08:06.267
-"You got any Funyuns, dude?
All right."

00:08:06.267 --> 00:08:07.334
Uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.334 --> 00:08:08.767
That didn't happen to me.

00:08:08.767 --> 00:08:10.501
Oh, well,
here's the free space --

00:08:11.767 --> 00:08:13.000
Okay, well, that's --

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.033
Everyone gets that one.

00:08:14.033 --> 00:08:15.801
Everyone gets that one,
of course.

00:08:15.801 --> 00:08:17.000
The next square says...

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.100
-Oh.
-Not this year.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.400
Not this year, thankfully.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.734
-Last year.
-Yeah, last year.

00:08:25.734 --> 00:08:28.067
That's a different story.
How about this one?

00:08:31.701 --> 00:08:33.234
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.234 --> 00:08:35.367
-"What do you know?
What do you know?"

00:08:35.367 --> 00:08:37.367
That didn't happen to me.
How about this one here?

00:08:41.367 --> 00:08:45.133
Yeah, actually did happen to me.
I'll take that one.

00:08:45.133 --> 00:08:47.667
Uh, and finally...

00:08:50.434 --> 00:08:52.200
Oh, that's --
Hey, I got Bingo!

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:55.367
-Yeah!
-I got Thanksgiving Bingo!

00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:56.934
All right.

00:08:56.934 --> 00:08:59.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:59.367 --> 00:09:01.901
Guys, today is a day
all about giving thanks,

00:09:01.901 --> 00:09:04.067
so why not a better day
to write out my weekly

00:09:04.067 --> 00:09:05.667
Thank You Notes right now?
You guys mind?

00:09:05.667 --> 00:09:06.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:06.868 --> 00:09:09.200
Oh, I'd love to.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.767
James, can I get some

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:12.734
Thank You Note writing music,
please?

00:09:12.734 --> 00:09:14.634
♪♪

00:09:14.634 --> 00:09:16.133
-Wow.

00:09:16.133 --> 00:09:19.033
♪♪

00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:20.467
Thankful.

00:09:20.467 --> 00:09:22.033
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.033 --> 00:09:23.601
♪♪

00:09:23.601 --> 00:09:25.734
-Thank you,
Thanksgiving leftovers,

00:09:25.734 --> 00:09:28.634
for leading to an epic game
of Fridge Tetris.

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:30.767
[ Laughs ]

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.567
[ Applause ]

00:09:35.234 --> 00:09:36.400
♪♪

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:39.067
Thank you,
canned cranberry sauce,

00:09:39.067 --> 00:09:40.901
for being the only thing
that keeps its shape

00:09:40.901 --> 00:09:42.534
after Thanksgiving.

00:09:42.534 --> 00:09:44.934
Yeah. Can't mess with that.

00:09:44.934 --> 00:09:48.067
I like --

00:09:48.067 --> 00:09:50.334
I like a good dessert
to have -- that has abs.

00:09:50.334 --> 00:09:51.767
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:09:54.367 --> 00:09:55.667
♪♪

00:09:55.667 --> 00:09:58.067
-Thank you, World Cup trophy.
-Ooh.

00:09:58.067 --> 00:10:00.267
-Because everyone knows
the first rule of soccer

00:10:00.267 --> 00:10:02.167
is hold the ball with two hands.

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:04.000
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.534 --> 00:10:07.033
Wait. What?
-What?

00:10:07.033 --> 00:10:09.100
[ Applause ]

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:10.534
♪♪

00:10:10.534 --> 00:10:13.334
-Thank you, peeling potatoes,
for either being a sign

00:10:13.334 --> 00:10:16.701
that you're helping Mom or did
something wrong in boot camp.

00:10:16.701 --> 00:10:18.968
[ Applause ]

00:10:21.133 --> 00:10:23.467
"Beetle Bailey!"
-"Get over here!"

00:10:24.767 --> 00:10:26.133
♪♪

00:10:26.133 --> 00:10:28.767
-Thank you, Thanksgiving,
for being that special day

00:10:28.767 --> 00:10:31.033
when your family is either upset
you're not married

00:10:31.033 --> 00:10:33.434
or upset about
who you did marry.

00:10:33.434 --> 00:10:35.267
[ Laughs ]

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:38.934
[ Applause ]

00:10:38.934 --> 00:10:40.901
"He's a loozah!"

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.334
♪♪

00:10:44.334 --> 00:10:46.367
Thank you,
airport X-ray machine,

00:10:46.367 --> 00:10:48.534
for letting me work off
Thanksgiving

00:10:48.534 --> 00:10:50.767
by doing one very slow
jumping jack.

00:10:50.767 --> 00:10:53.300
[ Laughter ]

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.334
[ Applause ]

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.834
♪♪

00:11:03.834 --> 00:11:06.634
Thank you, family photos,
for letting me remember

00:11:06.634 --> 00:11:10.434
exactly what mood each family
member was in at the time.

